 "model": "lora",
 "stop": "20 lines",
 "poem": "On his best colt, without a\nWhistle of alarm he crept along.\nHis wife came forth from her booth.  Instead\nOf the usual cup and pitcher\nHer dark eyes shone upon the stranger,\nAnd he recognized himself.\n\"Good-morning,\" she said.  \"How many\nHave you gone? how much time have taken?\nYou are too lazy to answer\nThe call of nature! I cannot\nProve it in so great a degree!\"  She\nJoined him at the door; upon\nTheir knees they wept together again.\nHe tried to join them with another\nLittle child's handkerchief over\nHer wet hair that ruffled about,\nBut her light fingers grasped not lightly,\nAnd she turned away before he\nWas ready to reach for another\nIn order to be comfort.",
